0result.sql
```

Reason:  
0result.sql identifies each legislator’s first term with MIN(term_start) instead of assuming term_number = 0, so every member of the 1917‑1999 cohort is captured even if early term_number data are missing.  It also treats open‑ended service with COALESCE(term_end,'9999‑12‑31') and counts DISTINCT legislators, guaranteeing one count per person.  Consequently its retention rates are reliable for the full cohort, whereas 2result.sql could drop legislators whose earliest row is not numbered 0.